  "corpusId": "northwind-sql-v1",
  "comment": "Agent I's SQL-bearing scenario set. Queries were written by a separate blind subagent that saw only a one-line intent per card (never the SQL, the card names except for exact-name slots, or any strategy text). Slots, split and labels are frozen in sql-slots.json. SPLIT RULE (frozen 2026-09-23 before any question text, strategy text or measurement existed): slots are grouped into 7 strata by id prefix (sqlc, sqlp, sqlr, mbql, desc, exact, fam); within a stratum slots are numbered 1..n in the listed order; slot n goes to HELD-OUT iff n mod 5 is 2 or 4, else DEV. Result: 24 held-out / 36 dev (40%). Held-out numbers are the headline; dev is for iterating. The split is carried as tags split-dev / split-heldout. LABELS: grades were assigned from the corpus alone before any question text was seen: target = 2, cards answering substantially the same need = 1; near-miss siblings are deliberately unlabelled (they count as not relevant).",
